      {
        "narration": "Sam keeps stats for his basketball team. In one game he made 1 of his 4 free throws. As a fraction, that is 1/4.",
        "text": "1/4",
        "visual": { "kind": "emoji", "emoji": "🏀", "count": null, "filled": null }
      },
      {
        "narration": "His coach likes percents. The word percent means out of 100. So 1% is 1 out of 100. That is the fraction 1/100, or the decimal 0.01.",
        "text": "1% = 1/100 = 0.01",
        "visual": null
      },
      {
        "narration": "To change 1/4 into a percent, make the denominator 100. Multiply 4 by 25 to get 100. Multiply the numerator by 25 too. So 1/4 is equivalent to 25/100.",
        "text": "1/4 = 25/100",
        "visual": null
      },
      {
        "narration": "Now read 25/100 three ways. It is 25 hundredths, so the decimal is 0.25. It is 25 out of 100, so the percent is 25%.",
        "text": "1/4 = 0.25 = 25%",
        "visual": null
      },
      {
        "narration": "You can also divide the numerator by the denominator. 1 ÷ 4 equals 0.25. That matches. Both ways name the same amount.",
        "text": "1 ÷ 4 = 0.25",
        "visual": null
      },
      {
        "narration": "Try 4/5. Multiply the numerator and the denominator by 20. You get 80/100. So 4/5 is 0.80, or 80%.",
        "text": "4/5 = 80/100 = 80%",
        "visual": null
      },
      {
        "narration": "A fraction, a decimal, and a percent can all name one amount. Let's practise changing between them.",
        "text": null,
        "visual": null
      }
    ],
